The reply states that "we have applied a one-time courtesy waiver to this fee," but according to the account record, a courtesy waiver was already applied on 2027-06-25. The fee was assessed on 2028-02-08, which is within twelve calendar months of the previous waiver (approximately 7 months later). Per the fee schedule, "A courtesy waiver applied fewer than twelve calendar months before the fee date bars a new one." Therefore, the borrower is not eligible for a new courtesy waiver, and the fee should stand. The reply's waiver status (stating the waiver was applied and the fee reversed) contradicts what the account record and policy dictate.

