The reply states "This fee cannot be waived" and "The late fee will remain on your account," but this conclusion is incorrect. According to the fee schedule, the borrower is enrolled in autopay (since 2025-11-04). The previous courtesy waiver was applied on 2027-01-28, and the current fee was assessed on 2028-02-16. Since more than twelve calendar months have passed between 2027-01-28 and 2028-02-16, the borrower is eligible for a new courtesy waiver. The reply's waiver status (that the fee cannot be waived and must remain) contradicts what the account record and fee schedule indicate should apply.

