The reply states that the late fee "will be reversed" under the hardship plan, which is correct according to HB-2027-12. However, the reply says "Your approved hardship plan covers this payment," which is misleading. The hardship plan was approved on 2028-03-01, but the payment triggering the fee was due on 2028-02-02 and posted on 2028-02-27—both before the hardship plan was approved. The fee is waived because the hardship plan retroactively covers the trigger payment, not because the plan "covers" the payment in the normal sense. This explanation is factually wrong about the relationship between the payment and the hardship plan timing, and borrowers must be told something true about why their fee is waived.
